<section class=3D"slide" id=3D"s11">
  <span class=3D"slide-tag">PART II =C2=B7 DSPY</span>
  <h1 class=3D"slide-title">DSPy: <em>"programming, not prompting"</em></h1=
>

  <p class=3D"lede">
    Stop hand-engineering brittle prompt strings. Declare what you want as =
a typed signature; let DSPy <em>compile</em> the prompt =E2=80=94 including=
 few-shot demos, instructions, and chain-of-thought scaffolds =E2=80=94 aga=
inst a metric on real data.
  </p>

  <div class=3D"grid-2">
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">THE PROBLEM</div>
      <h4>Prompt brittleness</h4>
      <p>Swap GPT-4o =E2=86=92 Claude =E2=86=92 Llama and your handcrafted =
prompt loses 10=E2=80=9330 points. Re-tune by hand. Repeat for every task.<=
/p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">THE INSIGHT</div>
      <h4>Prompts are parameters</h4>
      <p>Treat instructions and demonstrations as learnable. Define modules=
 with clear input/output contracts. Optimize the parameters automatically.<=
/p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">THE INTERFACE</div>
      <h4>Signature =E2=86=92 Module =E2=86=92 Optimizer</h4>
      <p>A signature is a typed I/O spec. A module is a callable LM program=
. An optimizer (teleprompter) tunes the program against a metric.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">THE OUTPUT</div>
      <h4>A compiled program</h4>
      <p>Portable across LMs. Re-compile in minutes when you swap models. V=
ersioned, diffable, testable.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"slide-num">11 / 44</div>
</section>

