=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D -->
<section class=3D"slide" id=3D"s15">
  <span class=3D"slide-tag">DSPY =C2=B7 COMPILATION</span>
  <h1 class=3D"slide-title">Compilation =3D <em>gradient-free</em> program =
synthesis</h1>

  <p class=3D"body">A teleprompter takes <code>(student_program, trainset, =
metric)</code> and returns a <em>compiled</em> program with optimized instr=
uctions and demonstrations. Conceptually, it solves a discrete optimization=
 in three families:</p>

  <div class=3D"step-flow">
    <div class=3D"step">
      <div class=3D"step-num">FAMILY A</div>
      <div class=3D"step-title">Demo selection</div>
      <div class=3D"step-desc">Search over which (input, output) traces to =
use as few-shot exemplars. Bootstrap, LabeledFewShot, KNNFewShot.</div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"step">
      <div class=3D"step-num">FAMILY B</div>
      <div class=3D"step-title">Instruction synthesis</div>
      <div class=3D"step-desc">Use an LM to propose better natural-language=
 instructions. COPRO, MIPROv2, GEPA.</div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"step">
      <div class=3D"step-num">FAMILY C</div>
      <div class=3D"step-title">Weight finetuning</div>
      <div class=3D"step-desc">Distill or finetune the underlying LM on boo=
tstrapped traces. BootstrapFinetune, Ensemble.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"callout">
    "Compilation" is exact: the teleprompter mutates a tree of <code>Predic=
t</code> objects in-place by setting <code>.demos</code> and <code>.signatu=
re.instructions</code>, then returns the program. You can <code>pickle</cod=
e> the result.
  </div>
  <div class=3D"slide-num">15 / 44</div>
</section>

