<!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D -->
<section class=3D"slide" id=3D"s37">
  <span class=3D"slide-tag">PRODUCTION =C2=B7 PATTERNS</span>
  <h1 class=3D"slide-title">Five patterns that <em>scale</em></h1>

  <div class=3D"grid-2">
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 01</div>
      <h4>Compile once, deploy many</h4>
      <p>Save compiled programs as JSON artifacts. Version them in git. Rol=
l back like any other model artifact. Treat re-compilation as a CI/CD step =
triggered on data drift.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 02</div>
      <h4>Two-tier LM</h4>
      <p>Strong <em>prompt_model</em> (Opus) for the proposer at compile ti=
me. Cheap <em>task_model</em> (Sonnet, Haiku) at inference. The expensive m=
odel never runs in prod.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 03</div>
      <h4>Metric as code</h4>
      <p>Your composite metric IS the spec. Code-review it. Test it on adve=
rsarial examples. Track its agreement with human judgment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 04</div>
      <h4>AutoRAG =E2=86=92 DSPy handoff</h4>
      <p>Let AutoRAG select chunker/retriever/reranker. Export the topology=
. Let DSPy take over for query-rewriter + generator + judge with that fixed=
 topology.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 05</div>
      <h4>Refusal as a first-class output</h4>
      <p>Always include a "can_answer" or "confidence" field. Compile again=
st a metric that rewards correct refusal as much as correct answers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <div class=3D"num">PATTERN 06</div>
      <h4>Trace logging</h4>
      <p>In prod, log every predictor's full input/output. Failures become =
next compile's trainset. The pipeline learns from itself.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"slide-num">37 / 44</div>
</section>

