<section class=3D"slide" id=3D"s38">
  <span class=3D"slide-tag">PRODUCTION =C2=B7 ANTI-PATTERNS</span>
  <h1 class=3D"slide-title">What goes wrong in <em>real</em> deployments</h=
1>

  <table class=3D"tech">
    <thead><tr><th>Anti-pattern</th><th>Why it fails</th><th>Fix</th></tr><=
/thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Tiny trainset (&lt; 30)</td>
        <td>Bootstrap finds 0 successes; teleprompter has nothing to learn =
from</td>
        <td>Synthesize examples (use Opus to generate from a seed), then hu=
man-validate</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Single-LM judge metric</td>
        <td>Optimizer learns to game the judge</td>
        <td>Use 3-judge consensus or program-of-thought verification</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Optimizing on a leaky metric</td>
        <td>Metric correlates with surface form, not truth</td>
        <td>Add adversarial examples; check metric's discrimination ability=
</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Re-compiling on every commit</td>
        <td>$50=E2=80=93$100 per CI run; nondeterministic</td>
        <td>Pin compile to data-version triggers, not code triggers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>"Heavy" budget by default</td>
        <td>Burns money for marginal gain after light/medium</td>
        <td>Always run light =E2=86=92 measure lift =E2=86=92 escalate</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Mixing AutoRAG and DSPy on same prompt</td>
        <td>Two optimizers disagree; one undoes the other's work</td>
        <td>Topology in AutoRAG; LM-stage prompts in DSPy. Strict separatio=
n.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Ignoring temperature</td>
        <td>Bootstrap at temp=3D0 misses diverse demos; production at temp=
=3D1 hallucinates</td>
        <td>Compile at temp=3D0.7 (proposer) / 0.0 (task); deploy at temp=
=3D0.0</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class=3D"slide-num">38 / 44</div>
</section>

